  </read_first>
  
  <action>
**Three modifications to MainWindow.xaml.cs:**

**Modification 1: ApplySettings — add UpdateModifierConfig call**

After line 317 (`_ghostMode.GhostFadeRadiusPx = s.GhostFadeRadiusPx;`), insert exactly:

```csharp
        _ghostMode.UpdateModifierConfig(s.UseCtrl, s.UseAlt, s.UseShift);
```

This initializes controller with modifier config from settings.json on app startup (INT-03).

**Modification 2: GetCurrentSettingsSnapshot — add modifier field mappings**

After line 405 (`GhostFadeRadiusPx = _ghostMode.GhostFadeRadiusPx,`), insert exactly:

```csharp
        UseCtrl                = _settings.UseCtrl,
        UseAlt                 = _settings.UseAlt,
        UseShift               = _settings.UseShift,
```

This exposes modifier config to Settings window for checkbox population (CFG-02).

**Modification 3: Fix two IsCtrlAltHeld call sites**

Line 1065 in Window_MouseEnter — replace:
```csharp
        if (_ghostMode.IsCtrlAltHeld() || !_ghostMode.IsEnabled)
```
with:
```csharp
        if (_ghostMode.IsModifierHeld() || !_ghostMode.IsEnabled)
```

Line 1539 in Window_PreviewMouseRightButtonUp — replace:
```csharp
        if (!RightClickMenuGate.ShouldOpen(_isDragging, _ghostMode.IsActive, _ghostMode.IsCtrlAltHeld()))
```
with:
```csharp
        if (!RightClickMenuGate.ShouldOpen(_isDragging, _ghostMode.IsActive, _ghostMode.IsModifierHeld()))
```

These call sites invoke the refactored IsModifierHeld method from Phase 83 (DET-01).

**Why these exact changes:** ApplySettings is the single initialization point before window shows (runs once on startup). GetCurrentSettingsSnapshot is called by OpenSettings + ResetToDefaults to populate/refresh UI. The two call sites use IsModifierHeld to suppress ghost fade when modifiers are held (Window_MouseEnter normal hover path, RightClickMenuGate right-click menu logic).
  </action>
  
