<task type="auto">
  <name>Task 2: Wire OpenSettings event subscriptions + extend ResetToDefaults</name>
  
  <read_first>
    - FuzzyClock.App/MainWindow.xaml.cs (lines 423-530 for OpenSettings event subscriptions, lines 1202-1288 for ResetToDefaults)
    - FuzzyClock.App/SettingsWindow.xaml.cs (verify UseCtrlChanged/UseAltChanged/UseShiftChanged event declarations from Phase 82)
    - FuzzyClock.App/GhostModeController.cs (lines 97-102 for UpdateModifierConfig signature)
  </read_first>
  
  <action>
**Two modifications to MainWindow.xaml.cs:**

**Modification 1: OpenSettings — add 3 event subscriptions**

After line 481 (`_settingsWindow.GhostFadeRadiusPxChanged += v => { _ghostMode.GhostFadeRadiusPx = v; SaveSettings(); };`), insert exactly:

```csharp
        // v4.3 Phase 84 — Modifier override configuration (INT-01, INT-02)
        _settingsWindow.UseCtrlChanged += v =>
        {
            _settings = _settings with { UseCtrl = v };
            SaveSettings();
            _ghostMode.UpdateModifierConfig(_settings.UseCtrl, _settings.UseAlt, _settings.UseShift);
        };
        _settingsWindow.UseAltChanged += v =>
        {
            _settings = _settings with { UseAlt = v };
            SaveSettings();
            _ghostMode.UpdateModifierConfig(_settings.UseCtrl, _settings.UseAlt, _settings.UseShift);
        };
        _settingsWindow.UseShiftChanged += v =>
        {
            _settings = _settings with { UseShift = v };
            SaveSettings();
            _ghostMode.UpdateModifierConfig(_settings.UseCtrl, _settings.UseAlt, _settings.UseShift);
        };
```

This pattern follows existing event subscriptions (immediate persistence via `_settings = _settings with {...}; SaveSettings();` then UpdateModifierConfig to propagate runtime change to controller). Each handler updates one field then passes all three current values to UpdateModifierConfig (INT-01, INT-02).

**Modification 2: ResetToDefaults — add modifier reset**

After line 1232 (`_ghostMode.GhostFadeRadiusPx = 80;`), insert exactly:

```csharp
        _ghostMode.UpdateModifierConfig(true, true, false);  // INT-04: restore Ctrl+Alt defaults
```

Then after line 1277 (inside the `_settings = _settings with {...}` block for Temps), add to the with-expression:

```csharp
            // v4.3 Phase 84 — Reset modifier override to Ctrl+Alt defaults (INT-04)
            UseCtrl  = true,
            UseAlt   = true,
            UseShift = false,
```

This ensures both controller state (via UpdateModifierConfig) AND persisted state (via _settings with-expression) reset to Ctrl+Alt defaults (true, true, false) matching CFG-04 init defaults (INT-04).

**Why these exact changes:** OpenSettings is the single location where all Settings window events get subscribed. ResetToDefaults must reset both runtime controller state (UpdateModifierConfig) and persisted state (_settings record) to maintain consistency. Pattern matches existing GhostFadeRadiusPx at line 1232 (controller property + settings field reset in tandem).
  </action>
  
