<task type="checkpoint:human-verify" gate="blocking">
  <name>Task 3: Human verification — end-to-end modifier configuration</name>
  
  <what-built>
Configurable ghost override wired end-to-end: Settings checkboxes persist immediately and update runtime behavior, Reset to Defaults restores Ctrl+Alt, all-unchecked disables override, full modifier combination matrix works correctly.
  </what-built>
  
  <how-to-verify>
**Run the application and complete this 8-category checklist:**

**Category 1: Startup Initialization (INT-03)**
1. Close app if running
2. Open `%LOCALAPPDATA%\FuzzyClock\settings.json`
3. Verify `"UseCtrl": true, "UseAlt": true, "UseShift": false` present (or absent — init defaults handle upgrade)
4. Launch app
5. Open Settings > Behavior > Ghost Override panel
6. Verify checkboxes show: Ctrl ☑ / Alt ☑ / Shift ☐
7. **Expected:** Checkbox state matches settings.json (or init defaults if fields absent)

**Category 2: Checkbox State Persistence (INT-02, TST-04 item 1)**
8. Uncheck "Left Ctrl" checkbox
9. Close Settings window
10. Close app completely
11. Relaunch app
12. Open Settings > Behavior > Ghost Override panel
13. Verify "Left Ctrl" is still unchecked (☐)
14. **Expected:** Checkbox state persisted across restart

**Category 3: Reset to Defaults (INT-04, TST-04 item 2)**
15. With Settings window open, uncheck all three modifiers (Ctrl ☐ / Alt ☐ / Shift ☐)
16. Close Settings window
17. Right-click widget → Reset to Defaults
18. Open Settings > Behavior > Ghost Override panel
19. Verify checkboxes show: Ctrl ☑ / Alt ☑ / Shift ☐
20. **Expected:** Reset restores Ctrl+Alt default configuration

**Category 4: All-Unchecked Behavior (DET-02, TST-04 item 3)**
21. Uncheck all three modifiers (Ctrl ☐ / Alt ☐ / Shift ☐)
22. Close Settings window
23. Hover cursor over widget
24. Hold Left Ctrl + Left Alt simultaneously while hovering
25. **Expected:** Widget fades to 0% opacity (ghost activates) despite held modifiers
26. Release modifiers, cursor still hovering
27. **Expected:** Widget remains at 0% opacity (override disabled means modifiers ignored)

**Category 5: Ctrl-only Configuration (DET-03, TST-04 item 4)**
28. Open Settings > Behavior > Ghost Override
29. Set: Ctrl ☑ / Alt ☐ / Shift ☐
30. Close Settings
31. Hover widget WITHOUT holding any keys
32. **Expected:** Widget fades (ghost activates)
33. Retreat cursor outside proximity zone, then hover again while holding Left Ctrl
34. **Expected:** Widget stays at 100% opacity (Ctrl suppresses fade)
35. Release Ctrl while still hovering
36. **Expected:** Widget fades immediately

**Category 6: Alt-only Configuration (DET-03, TST-04 item 5)**
37. Open Settings > Behavior > Ghost Override
38. Set: Ctrl ☐ / Alt ☑ / Shift ☐
39. Close Settings
40. Hover widget while holding Left Alt
41. **Expected:** Widget stays visible (Alt suppresses fade)
42. Hover widget while holding Left Ctrl (Alt NOT held)
43. **Expected:** Widget fades (Ctrl not enabled in config)

**Category 7: Multiple Modifiers AND Logic (DET-03, TST-04 item 6)**
44. Open Settings > Behavior > Ghost Override
45. Set: Ctrl ☑ / Alt ☑ / Shift ☐
46. Close Settings
47. Hover widget while holding ONLY Left Ctrl (Alt NOT held)
48. **Expected:** Widget fades (requires BOTH Ctrl AND Alt)
49. Hover widget while holding Left Ctrl + Left Alt simultaneously
50. **Expected:** Widget stays visible (both enabled modifiers held)

**Category 8: Ghost Mode Master Toggle (UI-03, TST-04 item 7)**
51. Open Settings > Behavior
52. Uncheck "Ghost Mode" master checkbox
53. Verify Ghost Override panel becomes grayed out (disabled)
54. Try clicking modifier checkboxes
55. **Expected:** Checkboxes are non-interactive (panel disabled when Ghost Mode off)
56. Re-check "Ghost Mode"
57. Verify Ghost Override panel becomes enabled again
58. **Expected:** Panel state follows master toggle

**Build + Test Verification:**
59. Run `dotnet build --no-restore` in terminal
60. Verify: Build Succeeded, 0 Error(s), 0 Warning(s)
61. Run `dotnet test --no-restore`
62. Verify: Test run complete, 0 Failed (expected ~566 passed total)
